    "Scouting Notes": "POST DRAFT NOTES\n Sits 92-95 on his fastball with 18” of vertical break from a 5.6’ release. \n Pounds the zone with the pitch, and is still had a whiff rate over 30% on it\n Low 80s slider with 4” of cut, that I wonder if they try to make a cutter with some more velo in pro ball\n Upper 70s curveball with a two plane shape that had a 42% whiff rate last year, but is pretty low spin and not sure it'll play all that well in pro ball as currently constructed\n Change up is my favorite secondary by quite a bit, he takes about 10 mph off of his fastball with 6” of vertical and 12” of arm side\n Really great feel for pitching, and throws a ton of strikes. There's data to like, but also old school pitchability here too. Could be a fun combo",
